{
  "title": "ONNX export of atan2 produces different result thantorch.atan2when input is zero",
  "issue_id": "162570",
  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\n`torch.atan2(x, y)` returns zero when both inputs are zero. The ONNX [decomposition of atan2](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/1c16c18a534d320d101ebb10c88bdf57cf84b3b1/torch/onnx/_internal/torchscript_exporter/symbolic_opset9.py#L739) produces NaN in this case. This issue also affects `torch.angle` which decomposes to `torch.atan2(x.imag, x.real)`. \n\nI encountered this issue when debugging an issue with an ONNX export of the Kokoro TTS model ([original issue](https://github.com/robertknight/rten/pull/928#issuecomment-3273328165)).\n\n**Reproduction:**\n\n```py\nimport onnxruntime as ort\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\n\n\nclass Net(nn.Module):\n    def forward(self, x, y):\n        return torch.atan2(x, y)\n\n\nnet = Net()\nx = torch.tensor([0.0])\ny = torch.tensor([0.0])\ntorch.onnx.export(\n    net, (x, y), \"atan2.onnx\", input_names=[\"x\", \"y\"], output_names=[\"output\"]\n)\n\nsess = ort.InferenceSession(\"atan2.onnx\")\n\ntorch_result = net(x, y)\nort_result = sess.run([\"output\"], {\"x\": x.numpy(), \"y\": y.numpy()})[0]\n\nprint(\"torch_result\", torch_result) # tensor([0.])\nprint(\"ort_result\", ort_result) # [nan]\n```\n\n### Versions\n\nCollecting environment information...\nPyTorch version: 2.7.1\nIs debug build: False\nCUDA used to build PyTorch: None\nROCM used to build PyTorch: N/A\n\nOS: macOS 15.6.1 (arm64)\nGCC version: Could not collect\nClang version: 17.0.0 (clang-1700.0.13.5)\nCMake version: version 4.0.2\nLibc version: N/A\n\nPython version: 3.12.11 (main, Jun  3 2025, 15:41:47) [Clang 17.0.0 (clang-1700.0.13.3)] (64-bit runtime)\nPython platform: macOS-15.6.1-arm64-arm-64bit\nIs CUDA available: False\nCUDA runtime version: No CUDA\nCUDA_MODULE_LOADING set to: N/A\nGPU models and configuration: No CUDA\nNvidia driver version: No CUDA\ncuDNN version: No CUDA\nIs XPU available: False\nHIP runtime version: N/A\nMIOpen runtime version: N/A\nIs XNNPACK available: True\n\nCPU:\nApple M3 Pro\n\nVersions of relevant libraries:\n[pip3] mypy==1.8.0\n[pip3] mypy-extensions==1.0.0\n[pip3] numpy==1.26.4\n[pip3] onnx==1.17.0\n[pip3] onnxconverter-common==1.14.0\n[pip3] onnxruntime==1.22.1\n[pip3] onnxruntime-genai==0.8.2\n[pip3] onnxscript==0.2.2\n[pip3] torch==2.7.1\n[pip3] torchmetrics==1.7.2\n[pip3] torchvision==0.22.1\n[conda] Could not collect\n\ncc @justinchuby @titaiwangms",
